  "description": "Liquid drum & bass in F minor at 172 bpm: no four on the floor, the groove is the two-step break. The kick lands on the 1 and the 'and' of 3, the snare on 2 and 4 (a half-time feel at double tempo), and busy hats with ghost notes fill the sixteenths between, on a sampled jazz kit. The harmony moves around the circle of fourths in jazz chords (Fm9 Bbm9 Eb9 Abmaj7 Dbmaj7 Gm7b5 C7), so the eight-bar phrase keeps moving instead of looping two chords. A reese bass (two detuned saws, a slowly moving filter) holds the roots; a wide pad and FM keys carry the chords, the pad ducking under the kick. The form: an intro without drums, a build on the hats alone, the drop, a breakdown where the drums and bass leave, a second drop whose break changes (a ghosted snare, a pushed kick, the ride) and adds a plucked arpeggio, an outro thinning back to the pad.",
